==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Exalted Ganesha''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Ganesha''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Ganesha acts as an improved [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut]] because of his gargantuan DPS - even more when he is damaged. His Long Distance ability lets him take down powerful backliner enemies such as [[THE SLOTH]], [[Master A.]], [[Camelle]] and [[Calamary]], and can even let him attack the enemy base before defeating the boss!

Ganesha's low range to engage makes him vulnerable in stages with short-ranged quick attackers like [[Bore]] and [[R.Ost]], where it can be difficult to protect him. Use a support unit like [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] along with meatshields ([[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], etc.) to provide significant defense.

Unfortunately, his attack will only be triggered when an enemy is within 400 range, which can make his usage vary per situation and stage. However, his chances to strike are increased if he is well-protected even if enemies are knocked back. Ganesha's long-ranged strike combined with his insane attack power gives him the ability to clear multiple enemies instantly (excluding bosses); therefore, this gives short-ranged units an advantage with support.

==='''Talents'''===
The most important Talent to get for Ganesha is his strengthen upgrade, as when maxed, his DPS when damaged jumps to a whopping 9048 DPS, which is on par with [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shishilan Pasalan]] when strengthened!

His knockback immunity talent is up to personal preference; on one hand, Ganesha loses one of his methods of repositioning. On the other hand, it prevents his attack from being interrupted by knockback enemies, and more importantly, gives him a better matchup against [[Mr. Mole]]. Choose wisely, as if you purchase the talent, you have no way of reversing it.

His attack up talent works very well with his strengthen ability, as it allows his DPS to go even higher (up to 10858 DPS!), making it a worthwhile purchase.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Ganesha gains three talents, which are all insanely powerful for what they give you. Attack Frequency Up increases his DPS by a huge margin. With this, Strengthen and Attack Buff all maxed out, he gains a sizeable 26K DPS on top of the natural levels he's given to unlock these Ultra Talents, more than [[Kasli the Bane (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasli, Daughter of Chaos]] at the same level. This should be the first Ultra Talent to invest in, as it will skyrocket his DPS to unbelievable levels.

Wave Immunity on the other hand, isn't as useful, but is quite great especially in stages where [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can't take the heat. As for Freeze Immune, it is the least worth of the Ultra Talents, but it is tailor-made to specifically make him counter [[Henry]] better, which he can definitely do well at as he'll be able to get into his blindspot much better and snipe him from there.

==='''Orb'''===
Attack up effect Orb any trait for specialization, Berserker Orb for even more overall DPS.

